not an official OpenReader release.

Offline speech uses sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0), Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0),
and eSpeak-NG pronunciation components (GPL-3.0-or-later).
License copies are bundled under assets/licenses and visible in the app.
Other Flutter dependencies retain their respective licenses.

Corresponding sources and model resources:
  This client: OpenReader-Native-source.zip beside the APK download.
  https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
  https://pub.dev/packages/sherpa_onnx/versions/2.0.1
  https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
  https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M
  https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/tag/tts-models

The English offline pack is made from kokoro-multi-lang-v1_0.tar.bz2
without quantizing the model. Its upstream LICENSE and README are kept
in the pack. No cloud API keys, passwords, or licensed celebrity voices
are included.

To build the client, install Flutter and an Android SDK, run flutter pub get,
and use flutter run for a debug build. A release build requires your own
android/key.properties and signing keystore; private signing keys are
intentionally not included in the source archive.
